MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_001: Hm. This edge needs some work. Gotta take this\nto the blacksmith for its regular maintenance.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_002: Hello, Simon. What occupies you today?
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_003: Huh?!
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_004: Hm? Why unseat yourself?
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_005: Ah... I'd just taken my equipment off and was\ndoing a little maintenance.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_006: My sword was unsheathed, so that's where my\nfocus was. Sorry about that...
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_007: An untruth. The spirits say so. They say your\nsmile lies.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_008: My arrival has caused a pang of fear to arrive\nfor you.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_009: So, you're a mind reader. No wonder you scare folks.\nThere are all kinds of rumors, you know...
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_010: They say there's a vulkan who's been chief celestial\ngeneral for centuries. And she's deadly with a spear.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_011: You'd never guess any of that just looking at her,\nbut in truth, she's a cold-blooded killer in black.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_012: There's also a rumor that a certain Angel of Death\ncomes for fools who dare challenge the temple.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_013: I've been called that. My enemies wove it from\ntheir fear and dressed me in it.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_014: The other vulkans preferred simply "General Ninae."
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_015: I don't know if you're a god, a demon, or what, but\nI can tell you rank yourself higher than everyone else.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_016: I bet they're all scared of you. Just based off what\nI've heard.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_017: Like, for example, that chief celestial general Ninae\nworships an evil goddess named Yu Phas...
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_018: Hm?!
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_019: There is no evil in Yu Phas. Wipe up the insult you\ncarelessly spilled.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_020: That was just what I'd heard. I don't personally think\nYu Phas is evil.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_021: I'm a descendant of the children of Damascar who\nYu Phas saved, actually. No need to raise your spear.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_022: All is well, then. Just this once.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_023: Whew... Let my mouth go a bit too much there.\nThat spear came out like lightning.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_C_024: She's as dangerous as the rumors say, this\nBlack-Lace Ninae.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_001: How can it be amended? Ah. Thank you for the\nadvice. Still...
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_002: What's happening over there? Did she drop all\nthose spears?
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_003: Oh. It's Simon. *sigh*
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_004: Ugh... Why is she looking at me like a lost puppy?
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_005: Damn it... What seems to be the trouble,\nMiss Black-Lace Ninae?
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_006: If there's damage to any of the blades, that can be\nfixed with a little honing.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_007: Good. That's good. I am used to others at the temple\ndoing my upkeeping for me.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_008: You high-ranking vulkans... You should learn\nto take care of your own equipment.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_009: By the way, are things...alright between us?
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_010: You pointed a spear at me last time we talked.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_011: Things are placid between us. You explained all.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_012: You are a child of Damascar. The children of\nDamascar esteem Yu Phas. Is there more?
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_013: It's a bit of a complicated topic, to be honest...
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_014: Mercenaries are supposed to pray to Mars, to ask\nfor the blessings of the Bringer of War.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_015: With Yu Phas being the goddess of death, calling on\nher before battle is like asking for bad luck. It's risky.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_016: Too risky to trust? Then you distrust Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_017: It's not that. Nothing worth drawing a spear over.\nJust, I'm both a child of Damascar and a mercenary.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_018: I know Yu Phas was kind to my ancestors. I've also\ndone my research on the Cleansing of Damascar.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_019: But I always find myself seeking to avoid death,\nwhatever form it takes.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_020: I want to survive... I'll worry about making peace\nwith the gods when I'm dead.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_021: Human beliefs are so odd. There is a roiling chaos\nto them.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_022: Heh. I'm no priest. I don't know how to talk about\nthis kind of thing.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_023: But I trust you more. Because you don't distrust\nYu Phas.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_024: Right. Like I said, it's complicated. Man, talking to\nthis "Angel of Death" is like talking to a little kid...
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_025: I have elsewhere to go. Thank you for amending\nthe spears with me.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_026: Sure... No problem.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_027: Seems like I don't need to tiptoe around her.\nThat's good news, if I can count on her in a fight.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_028: Oof... Don't alarm yourself. I tripped only\na short distance.
MID_SE_Sim_Nin_B_029: IF I can count on her...